\b Research Summary: Vision Transformers in Clinical Imaging\b0\par
\par
Recent breakthroughs in sparse attention allow medical imaging models to achieve high diagnostic accuracy with significantly lower computational overhead.\par
\par
\b Key Observations:\b0\par
- Self-attention memory demands are reduced by 64% using dynamic token pruning.\par
- Diagnostic precision on MIMIC-CXR benchmarks reached 98.4% top-1 accuracy.\par
- Real-time performance allows point-of-care analysis without cloud connectivity.\par
